{"review":{"at":"2026-09-29T00:04:50-05:00","size":"full","verdict":"fix","findings":[{"n":1,"kind":"fix","text":"The column demos don't make their point at 1920 or 3440. At those widths the cards are only a few lines tall, so the \"hole\" under the short title in short/ is about 40px, and centred/ looks almost the same as short/ (see layouts-decide-short/sheet.png and layouts-decide-centred/sheet.png at 3440). Cap the row's width, or give the full columns more text, so the empty box is obvious and centring it is a visible change."},{"n":2,"kind":"fix","text":"Each demo is supposed to lead with one picture, but the pictures at the top can't be read. They are photos of only the demo box, not the whole page, laid two across at half width, so the 3440 shot is a strip of grey slivers (every demo sheet; `pictures()` in public/layouts/decide/demo.js:18-29). Either shoot the whole page at 1920 and 3440 and show one picture per row, or drop the pictures and let the live demo right below them be the picture."},{"n":3,"kind":"fix","text":"public/layouts/decide/shoot.mjs:4 imports Playwright by an absolute path that contains the owner's Windows user name. The global rule says not to write the owner's name into code, and the path only works on this one machine. Find the global node_modules folder at run time instead (for example with `npm root -g`)."},{"n":4,"kind":"fix","text":"The layout skill now has two lists that are both \"five questions\": the new \"Choosing a layout: five questions\" (.claude/skills/layout/SKILL.md, the added section) sits right above the existing \"The five questions\". A reader, or an agent told \"question 2\", can't tell which list is meant; demo.js:14 already says \"the layout skill, question 2\" and it is ambiguous. Give the new list a name that sets it apart, such as \"Choosing a layout (before sizing)\", and number the references to it."},{"n":5,"kind":"note","text":"\"questions.js is the one copy\" isn't true. questions.md is a hand-written copy and the skill has a prose copy, so there are three copies, which questions.js:1-3 itself admits (\"change all three\"). A three-line script that writes questions.md from questions.js would take away one of the copies that can fall out of step."},{"n":6,"kind":"note","text":"layouts-decide-servex/sheet.png is one narrow prose column, 84% empty at 3440. That is the very failure the worked example warns against, and the answer the reader wants (Tile wall) comes last, at answers.md:33. Put the five picks first, as five small cards (question → pick), with the reasoning one click down."},{"n":7,"kind":"note","text":"On /layouts/ the new link is a sentence of text part way down a long page (layouts/sheet.png; public/layouts/page.js:74). It can be found, but it is not shown. As the \"how to choose\" entry point, it would stand out more as a preview card near the top."},{"n":8,"kind":"note","text":"On /layouts/decide/ at 1920 the five question cards fill the first screen, and the demo previews start below the fold (layouts-decide/sheet.png). The order is right, but the one-sentence lead could say that the live demos are further down."},{"n":9,"kind":"note","text":"The left nav in the amount demo links to `#` (public/layouts/decide/amount/page.js:35), so clicking it does nothing. Real anchors to its sections would make the demo work the way it describes."},{"n":10,"kind":"note","text":"demo.js:1 imports `ul` and `li` and demo.js:56 re-exports them, but no page uses them. Delete both."}],"branch":"worktree/layout-system","head":"66a3c4fc62add489ab4aadc822cd2f9f0988434b","model":"claude-opus-5-5","cost":0.6383558,"file":"review.md"}}
