{"log": {"at": "2026-08-14T22:10:00-05:00", "msg": "The T menu lied. `panel(fn)` builds `new Panel({draw: fn})`, so `data.template` stays unset and the bar's menu reads Panel.defaults.template — \"blank\" — while a clock is drawn. There was no door for \"give me a panel showing X\", which is exactly what the ask said. `panel()` now takes a T name as well as a function: `panel(\"clock\")`. Two lines, no new export, and the call site reads like the request."}}
{"log": {"at": "2026-08-14T22:10:20-05:00", "msg": "The height is the knob, not the width. The clock is `font-size: min(17cqw, 38cqh)`, so in any band wider than tall the HEIGHT sizes it — a fixed --panel-height: 34em had the clock filling 74% of the band at 1280 and 32% at 3440, i.e. a 2986x612 box with 955px of clock in it. `clamp(20em, 26vw, 48em)` measures 54/51/46% at 1280/1920/3440 — one composition at every width, and the band grows with the screen instead of the gutters."}}
